        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cbab20ef-1a3c-5d06-b935-f40acbb00fe7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Il trovatore, La rondine, Doretta's Dream, El trovador, Rigoletto, Elena da Feltre\n- People: Giuseppe Verdi, Salvadore Cammarano, Antonio García Gutiérrez, Giacomo Puccini, Giuseppe Adami, Alfred Maria Willner, Pietro Neri-Baraldi\n- Places: Bologna, Teatro del Corso\n- Roles: Manrico, Duke of Mantua, Ubaldo\n\nFacts:\n- In 1836, Antonio García Gutiérrez wrote the play \"El trovador\".\n- Giuseppe Verdi's opera \"Il trovatore\" is an opera in four acts with an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano and based on Antonio García Gutiérrez's 1836 play \"El trovador\".\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi was engaged as the leading tenor at the Teatro del Corso.\n- By 1853, Pietro Neri-Baraldi sang in the first Bologna performances of \"Il trovatore\" as Manrico, \"Rigoletto\" as the Duke of Mantua, and \"Elena da Feltre\" as Ubaldo at the Teatro del Corso.\n- Giacomo Puccini's opera \"La rondine\" is an opera in three acts with an Italian libretto by Giuseppe Adami based on a libretto by Alfred Maria Willner and another collaborator not named in this chunk.\n- The song \"Doretta's Dream\" is based on \"Chi il bel sogno di Doretta,\" an aria from Giacomo Puccini's opera \"La Rondine\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "34a800ee-fc85-5509-826e-c33e07fc1389",
        "text": "Page: Il trovatore. Sentence: Il trovatore (] ; Italian for \"The Troubadour\") is an opera in four acts by Giuseppe Verdi to an Italian libretto largely written by Salvadore Cammarano, based on the play \"El trovador\" (1836) by Antonio García Gutiérrez.\nPage: La rondine. Sentence: La rondine (\"The Swallow\") is an opera in three acts by Giacomo Puccini to an Italian libretto by Giuseppe Adami, based on a libretto by Alfred Maria Willner and .\nPage: Pietro Neri-Baraldi. Sentence: By 1853 he was engaged as the leading tenor at the Teatro del Corso where he sang in the first performances in Bologna of \"Il trovatore\" (as Manrico), \"Rigoletto\" (as the Duke of Mantua), and \"Elena da Feltre\" (as Ubaldo).\nPage: Doretta's Dream. Sentence: The song is based on the aria \"Chi il bel sogno di Doretta\" (\"Doretta's Beautiful Dream\") from Giacomo Puccini's opera \"La Rondine\".",
